VDR Plugin 'hyperion' Revision History
--------------------------------------

2026-10-30: Version 0.1.0

- Initial revision.

2026-11-04: Version 0.2.0

- Use nlohmann/json for the messages of the JSON server (new build dependency,
  header only, 3.7 or newer).
- The setup page changes some settings of Hyperion itself (smoothing with time
  and delay, black border detection, brightness). They are read from and stored
  in the configuration of Hyperion (2.1 or newer) and written into every
  instance, only the changed values.
- Log in with the default password of Hyperion like its web interface, so the
  settings need no token as long as no password is set. The password is never
  guessed.
- Request a token from Hyperion in the setup: it is accepted in the web
  interface of Hyperion and stored at once.
- Search Hyperion in the local network (SSDP) and take over host and ports.
- Show test patterns on the screen and the leds (colors, edges, delay). With
  the delay pattern, the delay of the leds is changed live.
- New SVDRP command STAT: the state as "key: value" lines (e.g. for home
  automation).
- README: follow the TV with cecremote (SVDRP AMBI on CEC standby/power on).
- A failed request of the setup (e.g. a wrong token) doesn't delay the own
  JSON requests of the plugin anymore.

2026-11-04: Version 0.2.1

- ambientimage_service.h is under the MIT license, so other output plugins can
  provide the service.
- ambientimage_service.h describes the image exactly (byte order, range, color
  space, placement of the video) and reports a too small buffer
  (AMBIENT_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL).
- Enlarge the image buffer, if the output plugin needs more (e.g. a screen,
  which is higher than wide).
